new file mode 100644
index 0000000..65cad0d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SHORTREAL_SUBSET.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Experimental native shortreal compiler milestone
+
+This isolated compiler branch starts at Verilator v5.054 (`bbb60a403932a9f695cb6ff001ceb73de6ad9234`). It is not installed globally and is not used by the model server.
+
+The intended first milestone preserves a distinct FLOAT dtype, emits actual C++ float storage for internal scalars and fixed unpacked arrays, implements explicit narrowing/widening and 32-bit bit reinterpretation, and lowers add/subtract/multiply to dedicated FP32 AST nodes. DOUBLE remains the real/realtime dtype. This is compiler language support; generated code is not edited and no host neural kernel is substituted.
+
+IEEE 1800 section 11.3.1, also recorded in the official Accellera proposal at https://accellera.org/images/eda/sv-bc/att-6692/1035_D3a.htm, specifies real promotion when an operand is real, otherwise shortreal promotion when an operand is shortreal. Logical/relational results remain single-bit. Literal real constants are still real64; explicit shortreal casts establish FP32 operands. Assignment and cast boundaries must narrow explicitly. Each supported FP32 arithmetic node has an FP32 result. Generated simulation compilation must disable contraction and fast-math, preserving separate multiplication and addition rounding.
+
+The first milestone intentionally does not introduce a binary32 constant representation into V3Number. New FP32 nodes are not constant-folded; attempts to evaluate them in required constant-expression contexts produce an unsupported diagnostic. Runtime assignment from real literals remains supported. This avoids silently passing NaN payloads through the existing double-only constant representation. Constant folding is a later milestone with its own representation and tests.
+
+Initially rejected: shortreal ports and function signatures (including DPI), parameters/required constant expressions, trace, save, VPI and SystemC. Unsupported operators must be rejected instead of routed through integral widths or silently promoted to real64. The current work is incomplete until positive and negative tests establish these boundaries.
+
+Validation plan: distinguish32-bit/64-bit storage and `$bits`; test typedef and opposite array bounds, narrowing ties near2^24, widening, separate multiply/add, signed zero, subnormals, overflow, NaN bitcast payload, mixed-real promotion, and a small array dot. Run existing real/integer regressions unchanged. Only then inspect generated FP32 SIMD and consider a projection benchmark. No full model quality or speed conclusion follows from a compiler build.
+
+Local build uses CMake with the SDK FlexLexer header because autoconf is absent. Build products stay under ignored build-local. No dependency or global installation is required.
+
+First runtime status: t_shortreal_subset and unchanged upstream t_math_real passed with the first built compiler. The former checks bit patterns rather than host floating approximations. These passes precede the final rejection guards and optimized-code gate; the work is not yet a validated release. Independent review found and bounded wide integral conversion (double-rounding), wide bitcast, aggregate streaming, comparison promotion and unsupported operator gaps. The initial subset now intends to reject those cases explicitly, including integer conversions above32 bits. Direct integral-to-FP32 conversion is a future node, not approximated via double.
+
+The first handwritten scan of W8A8 code had missed dotted Apple instruction names; the FP32 inspection will explicitly count both dotted and conventional assembly mnemonics and identify the relevant hot function before making SIMD claims.
+
+Final bounded milestone: all11 selected tests pass (O0/O3 shortreal runtime, combined unsupported operators, standalone streaming/AND/modulus/integral-localparam rejects, and unchanged math_real, math_real_round, cast, math_signed). Separate negative fixtures run with -Wno-fatal so warnings cannot masquerade as feature rejection. The localparam fix checks expression content as well as declared dtype. Range/enum/generate-if uses of shortreal bitcasts also reject rather than reaching code generation. Independent review is required before archival acceptance.
+
+Optimized code contains actual FP32 scalar fmul/fadd and a two-lane fmul.2s in the array projection; the generated storage includes VlUnpacked<float,3>. This is a language/compiler milestone, not a performance result. No full-model conversion or quality validation has occurred. There is no commercial SV simulator comparison in this environment.
+
+Strict-rounding support is currently limited to the generated GNUmake build path, which appends -fno-fast-math -ffp-contract=off after user flags when FLOAT exists. This affects all arithmetic in that generated model, including embedded real64 operations. A fair speed comparison must compile the deployed FP64 worker separately using its original compiler and flags. Do not report a shared strict-FP model's slowed FP64 comparator as the production baseline. Other build generators/manual compilation must supply equivalent strict flags and are outside this validated milestone.
